	<h4><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/blog/2016/04/26/artist-censors-anti-war-mural-to-appease">Artist Censors Anti-war Mural to Appease 'Triggered' Student</a></h4>
		<p class="meta"><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/people/robby-soave">Robby Soave</a><span class="pipe">|</span><time datetime="2016-04-27T02:35:00+00:00">4.26.16</time></p>
</li>

	</ul>
</section>
																<section class="relatedtopics">
	<ul>
		<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/guns">Guns</a></li>
<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/gun-rights">Gun Rights</a></li>
<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/gun-control">Gun Control</a></li>
<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/california">California</a></li>
<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/new-york">New York</a></li>
<li><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/tags/regulation">Regulation</a></li>

	</ul>
	</section>
							</aside>
					</section>
															<p>Understanding the rejection requires understanding gun owners\xe2\x80\x99
shared experiences. Compromise requires that both parties
relinquish something. If your counterpart\xe2\x80\x99s position is \xe2\x80\x9cgive me
this now, and I\xe2\x80\x99ll take the rest later,\xe2\x80\x9d there is no real
compromise to be had. Over decades, that has been precisely the
experience of American gun owners.</p>
<p>Back in 1976, Pete Shields, chairman of what is today the Brady
Campaign, candidly laid out the blueprint for <em>The New
Yorker</em>:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We're going to have to take one step at a time, and the first
step is necessarily \xe2\x80\x94 given the political realities \xe2\x80\x94 going to be
very modest. Right now, though, we'd be satisfied not with half a
loaf but with a slice. Our ultimate goal \xe2\x80\x94 total control of
handguns in the United States \xe2\x80\x94 is going to take time. My estimate
is from seven to ten years. The problem is to slow down the
increasing number of handguns sold in this country. The second
problem is to get them all registered. And the final problem is to
make the possession of all handguns and all handgun ammunition \xe2\x80\x94
except for the military, policemen, licensed security guards,
licensed sporting clubs, and licensed gun collectors \xe2\x80\x94 totally
illegal.</p>
</blockquote>
									<aside class="ad">
					<div id="google_ads_div_Web_Article_mobile_middle1">
<script type="text/javascript">
googletag.cmd.push(function(){googletag.display("google_ads_div_Web_Article_mobile_middle1");});
</script>
</div>					</aside>


		<p>The group\xe2\x80\x99s first target was \xe2\x80\x9cSaturday Night Specials,\xe2\x80\x9d
inexpensive small revolvers, alleged to be criminals\xe2\x80\x99 preferred
gun. When that approach gained traction, Shields shifted to a
larger target, claim that criminals were now using \xe2\x80\x9cexpensive, but
small pistols,\xe2\x80\x9d so all small pistols had to be banned.
\xe2\x80\x9cConcealability is the key,\xe2\x80\x9d he now explained.</p>
<p>As the years passed, it became apparent that this was going
nowhere; a different first \xe2\x80\x9cslice\xe2\x80\x9d would have to be found. In 1990,
Violence Policy Center (VPC) announced that it had found it. The
debate must be switched from small handguns to large \xe2\x80\x9cassault
rifles.\xe2\x80\x9d</p>
<p>Handguns, VPC explained, had become a media and political
nonissue, while calls to outlaw \xe2\x80\x9cassault rifles\xe2\x80\x9d would benefit from
mistaken impressions, <em>i.e.</em>, \xe2\x80\x9cthe public's confusion over
fully automatic machine guns versus semi-automatic assault
weapons\xe2\x80\x94anything that looks like a machine gun is assumed to be a
machine gun.\xe2\x80\x9d That rifles <em>of all types</em> were involved in
about 300 homicides a year was beside the point. The search was for
a target of opportunity, not a solution to crime.</p>
<p>The major gun control organizations bought the idea, to the
point of changing their names to replace \xe2\x80\x9chandgun\xe2\x80\x9d with \xe2\x80\x9cgun.\xe2\x80\x9d Pete
Shields\xe2\x80\x99 group, Handgun Control, Inc., became the Brady Center to
Prevent Gun Violence. The National Coalition to Ban Handguns became
the Coalition To Stop Gun Violence.</p>
<p>The change underscored a lesson gun owners had already learned.
Their opponents would go for any target of opportunity\xe2\x80\x94if handgun
restrictions didn\xe2\x80\x99t fly, try to restrict rifles\xe2\x80\x94and use that as a
foundation to take more in the future. Any \xe2\x80\x9creasonable compromise\xe2\x80\x9d
would simply be a first step in a long campaign to make firearm
ownership as difficult, expensive, and legally risky as
possible.</p>
<p>Take the example of California. There, 1920s legislation
required a permit for concealed carry of a firearm, required
dealers to report handgun sales to the state, and imposed a one-day
waiting period for handgun sales.</p>
<p>The one-day wait was meant to impede \xe2\x80\x9ccrimes of passion,\xe2\x80\x9d but in
1955 it was increased to three days, in 1965 to five days, and in
1975 to 10 days.</p>
<p>Open carry of a firearm was initially allowed. In 1967, open
carrying of loaded guns was prohibited. In recent years, open
carrying even of unloaded guns was forbidden in incorporated areas.
The mere sight of an unloaded gun was apparently too much for the
California legislature to tolerate.</p>
<p>In 2001, dealers were forbidden to sell handguns that were not
approved by the government, after rigorous laboratory testing,
funded by the manufacturer. Every slight variation, even changes in
color or finish, required a new certification. The tests actually
had nothing to do with reliability or safety, as evidenced by the
exemption of law enforcement firearms from them.</p>
<p>Along the way, the state banned \xe2\x80\x9cassault weapons,\xe2\x80\x9d magazines
holding more than 10 rounds, and private gun sales that didn\xe2\x80\x99t go
through dealers. In 1999, \xe2\x80\x9cone gun a month\xe2\x80\x9d was enacted, for no
discernible reason (why would a gun runner pick the most tightly
regulated state in the West as his source?)</p>
<p>Today, the weapons regulation portion of the California Penal
Code Annotated spans over 1,050 pages, yet at last count 68 more
gun control measures are pending in the legislature. No matter how
much the advocates of gun control get, it will never be enough.</p>
<p>Or try New Jersey, which requires a license to own guns, plus a
separate permit for each handgun. Carrying open or concealed is in
practice forbidden (the legal standard for a permit is
\xe2\x80\x9c<em>urgent</em> necessity\xe2\x80\x9d), carrying of hollow-point bullets is
subject to complex rules, and magazines are limited to 15
rounds.</p>
<p>That\xe2\x80\x99s not enough, apparently, since the New Jersey legislature
is considering bills to cut the magazine limit to five rounds, and
to require psychiatric evaluations and home inspections before
issuance of the firearm ownership license. Recently three
legislators had an embarrassing \xe2\x80\x9chot mike\xe2\x80\x9d problem after a gun bill
hearing, in which someone proclaimed, \xe2\x80\x9cWe needed a bill that is
going to confiscate, confiscate, confiscate.\xe2\x80\x9d\xc2\xa0</p>
<p>Or try New York, long considered to have the strictest gun laws
in the country, including requiring pistol possession permits
(issued at the sole discretion of police, with application fees as
high as $340), carry permits limited in some jurisdictions to
government officials and celebrities, and a 10 round magazine
limit. Then came the Newtown slayings, and the legislature decided
it must do something more. The legislation it rushed through
reduced the allowed magazine capacity to seven rounds (effectively
outlawing the many firearms for which seven round magazines have
never been made), required background checks to buy ammunition, and
greatly broadened its \xe2\x80\x9cassault rifle ban.\xe2\x80\x9d</p>
<p>New York\xe2\x80\x99s Attorney General described this as \xe2\x80\x9cmodest first
step.\xe2\x80\x9d</p>
<p>So much for compromise.</p>
	</div>
</div>




