		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>That is a good question. I am frankly surprised they haven't
thought of that.</p>
<p>They would have a hard time putting giving up a federally
protected right as a condition to federal employment. I don't think
the courts would ever go for that. But if Heller were ever
overturned, the President could by a stroke of a pen make everyone
choose between gun ownership and their security clearance.</p>		</div>
