	<li class="com-block reply3" id="comment_3888261" data-comment-id="comment_3888261" data-user-id="7952" data-comment-timestamp="1374593319">
				<p class="meta"><strong>phwest</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-23T15:28:39+00:00">7.23.13 @ 11:28AM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3888261">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>Because cars are valuable pieces of property, broadly owned,
that are frequenty left unattended in public places. It is
generally in the interest of car owners to have a system that makes
it readily apparent that they own their vehicles and can provide an
obvious means of identification if stolen.</p>
<p>Registration is also used by the government as a means of
enforcing other laws (mandatory insurance being the main one), but
that was not why government registration was established in the
first place.</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
		<div class="commentactions">

							<button class="comment_reply submit" name="commentparent" value="3888261" style="display:none">reply to this</button>

