			<!--Comment Head-->
	<li class="com-block reply4" id="comment_3884823" data-comment-id="comment_3884823" data-user-id="18730" data-comment-timestamp="1374457619">
				<p class="meta"><strong>Enigma</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-22T01:46:59+00:00">7.21.13 @ 9:46PM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3884823">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<blockquote>Just quit whining about our government.</blockquote>
<p>Make me.</p>
<blockquote>"The people" have the opportunity to over throw our
government every four years.</blockquote>
<p>How insipid. The executive bureaucracies are not elected and
unaccountable. Our system is controlled by two major parties that
often times collude with big business and big labor to screw us out
of our money. Instead of offering solutions, they give us excuses,
lame and deceitful justifications of their corruption.</p>
<blockquote>The fact is "the people" have chosen.</blockquote>
<p>No, the fact is 50% of the country choose. The rest don't care
(perhaps because they know the system is rigged). Also I'm
interested, if "the people" choose, does that give them a right to
do whatever they want to the minority? I mean, democracy and all.
Right? Are the majority's views more virtuous because they are the
majority's views?</p>
<blockquote>Your views lost.</blockquote>
<p>People thought the world was flat for a long time. Those who
said otherwise were ridiculed. Their views lost at that time. (PS,
please tell this to a Stalinist or Maoist)</p>
<blockquote>A more coherent argument and less name calling will
make you more persuasive.</blockquote>
<p>This applies to all of your posts (and most left-wing and
conservative criticisms of libertarianism).</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
		<div class="commentactions">

