	<li class="com-block reply0" id="comment_3880561" data-comment-id="comment_3880561" data-user-id="14644" data-comment-timestamp="1374239319">
				<p class="meta"><strong>timbo</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-19T13:08:39+00:00">7.19.13 @ 9:08AM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3880561">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>I wish all sane, law abiding people had guns. Then crime would
be less and the criminal fucks in Washington would be less apt to
fuck with our freedom.</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
		<div class="commentactions">

							<button class="comment_reply submit" name="commentparent" value="3880561" style="display:none">reply to this</button>

			<p class="comment_reply_msg login" style="display:none"><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/users/login">log in</a> or <a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/users/register">register</a> to reply</p>
		</div>
			</li>



			<!--Comment Head-->
	<li class="com-block reply0" id="comment_3881068" data-comment-id="comment_3881068" data-user-id="8325" data-comment-timestamp="1374247072">
				<p class="meta"><strong>BambiB</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-19T15:17:52+00:00">7.19.13 @ 11:17AM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3881068">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>The American Revolution began as a result of British attempts at
gun control. It is not inconceivable that future efforts at gun
control may lead to the Second American Revolution.</p>
<p>Our government is balanced on the edge of a razor. The Federal
Reserve is churning out tens of billions of fiat dollars each
month, desperately trying to "stimulate" the economy. Each dollar
it prints devalues every other dollar in circulation, portending
rampant inflation. What will Americans do when their $50,000
incomes will only buy them a dozen loaves of bread? As the Country
circles the vortex of economic destruction at an ever-increasing
rate, the political masters are fervently plotting means to prevent
a citizen backlash that may well include violent revolt. To them,
it is ever more important to disarm the People they intend to rule
before those People dispossess them of power.</p>
<p>But how do you convince a third of the population to surrender
their right to bear arms?</p>
<p>This has been the intractable question for recent
administrations - one they are increasingly desperate to resolve.
Where previous efforts involved appeals to "reasonable" gun
control, recent efforts have been cruder and more devious.
(cont.)</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
