		</div>
			</li>



			<!--Comment Head-->
	<li class="com-block reply0" id="comment_3881071" data-comment-id="comment_3881071" data-user-id="8325" data-comment-timestamp="1374247085">
				<p class="meta"><strong>BambiB</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-19T15:18:05+00:00">7.19.13 @ 11:18AM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3881071">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>The Attorney General has presided over a program involving the
FBI, ICE, DEA, ATF and DOJ in a plot to drive up the number of
"American" guns found at Mexican crimes scenes (and thereby justify
more gun control in America) by shipping thousands of "assault
weapons" to Mexican drug cartels. These guns have been used to
murder hundreds of Mexican citizens and at least one American, and
will continue to be used in crime for many years to come. No
legitimate law-enforcement goal was served by this wholesale export
of arms to criminals. The president has exerted "executive
privilege" to cover up the details.</p>
<p>The DHS has ordered more than 1.5 BILLION rounds of ammunition
(enough to fight 25 years worth of wars) to dry up supplies and
raise the cost of ammunition. It should not escape anyone's
attention that the TYPE of ammunition being purchased costs twice
the price of suitable practice ammunition. Nor should anyone fail
to recognize that it cannot legally be used in wars with other
countries. This ammunition (hollow point) may only be used to kill
Americans - and DHS has ordered enough to shoot every American five
times. Is our government stupid enough to pay double for ammunition
ostensibly purchased in bulk as a "cost-saving" measure? Or is it
preparing to go to war with its citizens?</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
		<div class="commentactions">

							<button class="comment_reply submit" name="commentparent" value="3881071" style="display:none">reply to this</button>

			<p class="comment_reply_msg login" style="display:none"><a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/users/login">log in</a> or <a href="//web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://reason.com/users/register">register</a> to reply</p>
		</div>
			</li>



			<!--Comment Head-->
	<li class="com-block reply1" id="comment_3883301" data-comment-id="comment_3883301" data-user-id="18629" data-comment-timestamp="1374339750">
				<p class="meta"><strong>Ronald Reagan</strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-20T17:02:30+00:00">7.20.13 @ 1:02PM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3883301">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>"The American Revolution began as a result of British attempts
at gun control."</p>
<p>I thought it was about tea...</p>
<p>The genius of our system is the ability of citizens to overthrow
a government that they objet to by VOTING. The government that you
are whining about is the result of the system that the founding
fathers you worship put in place.</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
