			<!--Comment Head-->
	<li class="com-block reply2" id="comment_3883517" data-comment-id="comment_3883517" data-user-id="15687" data-comment-timestamp="1374355179">
				<p class="meta"><strong><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://www.jpfo.org/" rel="nofollow">James Solbakken</a></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-20T21:19:39+00:00">7.20.13 @ 5:19PM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3883517">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>"The genius of our system is the ability of citizens to
overthrow a government that they objet to by VOTING. The government
that you are whining about is the result of the system that the
founding fathers you worship put in place."<br/>
Some problems with that: Our Founders did NOT place a lot of faith
in voting. In fact, they had a LOT of critical things to say about
democracy in general. They considered the general LIMITATION of
government to be the most important factor in preserving the
people's liberty. Also, our Founders said flat out that when the
government THEY set up no longer served the People then the People
should ALTER AND/OR ABOLISH IT!!! See how stupid and ignorant you
really are? You got it all wrong!!!!</p>		</div>
		<!--Comment actions (Reply/Login/Register)-->
		<div class="commentactions">

							<button class="comment_reply submit" name="commentparent" value="3883517" style="display:none">reply to this</button>

