	<li class="com-block reply0" id="comment_3881491" data-comment-id="comment_3881491" data-user-id="18947" data-comment-timestamp="1374254564">
				<p class="meta"><strong><a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160508032850/http://www.whatisgreatcinema.com/" rel="nofollow">Vincent Milburn</a></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><strong><time datetime="2013-07-19T17:22:44+00:00">7.19.13 @ 1:22PM</time></strong><span class="pipe">|</span><a class="permalink" href="#comment_3881491">#</a></p>

		<!--Comment Body-->
				<div class="content">
			<p>If gun control passes and crime goes down: "Hey, the gun
control's working! We should have more of it!</p>
<p>If gun control passes and crime goes up: "Oh, gee, the gun
control isn't quite working. We need more!"</p>
<p>No matter what outcome, we always need more gun control. It's
completely divorced from results.</p>
<p>The best thing we can do to stop crime is what we already do,
prosecute criminals.</p>		</div>
