		<article class="article">
			<div id="content_box">
									<div id="post-1637" class="g post post-1637 type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-uncategorized tag-gun-control tag-gun-debate tag-gun-rights has_thumb">
						<div class="single_post">
														<header>
								<h1 class="title single-title">10 Arguments For and Against Gun Control</h1>
															</header><!--.headline_area-->
<!-- Error, Ad is not available at this time due to schedule/geolocation restrictions! -->							<div class="post-single-content box mark-links">
																								<p><img class="alignleft size-full wp-image-1650" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20160331104550im_/http://www.thefinancialword.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Gun-Flag_730X350.jpg" alt="Gun-Flag_730X350" width="730" height="350" srcset="http://web.archive.org/web/20160331104550im_/http://www.thefinancialword.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Gun-Flag_730X350-300x144.jpg 300w, http://web.archive.org/web/20160331104550im_/http://www.thefinancialword.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Gun-Flag_730X350.jpg 730w" sizes="(max-width: 730px) 100vw, 730px"/><div class="a-single a-5"><div style="font-size: 0; display: block; float: right; margin-left: 40px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"><img class="alignnone wp-image-27 size-full" style="display: block;" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20160331104550im_/http://www.thefinancialword.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Advert300.gif" alt="Advertisement" width="300" height="21"/><style type="text/css">
.adslot_1 { width: 320px; height: 100px; }
@media (min-width:500px) { .adslot_1 { width: 336px; height: 280px; } }
</style>
<script async src="//web.archive.org/web/20160331104550js_/http://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js"></script>
<!-- TFW_ContentResp_336X280or320X100 -->
<ins class="adsbygoogle adslot_1" style="display:block" data-ad-client="ca-pub-7705704109170672" data-ad-slot="8791801747" data-ad-format="auto"></ins>
<script>
(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});
</script></div></div>For decades, gun control had been a secondary\xc2\xa0issue in presidential elections. But in the wake of an increasing number of mass, public shootings, 2016 presidential hopefuls are experiencing a dramatic shift, and candidates are being forced to talk more on gun control, which promises to become a far more influential factor in the coming election.</p>
<p>Clinton claims that silence on the issue is \xe2\x80\x9cthe height of irresponsibility\xe2\x80\x9d and with President Obama\xe2\x80\x99s recent executive action, stricter gun control laws have become the centerpiece of his late-term legacy. GOP candidates criticize the president\xe2\x80\x99s executive orders as doing too much to restrict the rights of law-abiding citizens. Marco Rubio has commented that the 2nd Amendment is \xe2\x80\x9ca cornerstone of our democracy,\xe2\x80\x9d and GOP frontrunner Donald Trump called Obama\xe2\x80\x99s plan \xe2\x80\x9cno good\xe2\x80\x9d and promised to \xe2\x80\x9cunsign\xe2\x80\x9d it if elected president.\xc2\xa0Here are ten of the most frequently discussed arguments on both sides of the issue.\xc2\xa0<span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>Where do you stand?</strong></span></p>
<h2><span style="color: red;">1) Stricter Gun Control Legislation is an Attack on the 2nd Amendment</span></h2>
<p><strong><span style="color: red;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Gun Rights Position:</span>\xc2\xa0</span></strong><br/>
A well regulated Militia, being necessary to the security of a free State, the right of the people to keep and bear Arms, shall not be infringed.&#8221; As detailed in the 2nd Amendment, our founding fathers saw the right to bear arms as a fundamental liberty of every law-abiding citizen. The Supreme Court has also affirmed a reading of the 2nd Amendment by which individual citizens have the fundamental right to own and bear arms for the purposes of self-defense against violence or tyranny.</p>
<p><strong><span style="color: blue;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Gun Control Position:</span><br/>
</span></strong>True, but the key words of the 2nd Amendment are \xe2\x80\x98a well regulated Militia,\xe2\x80\x99 which give us context for the meaning of the right to bear arms. The potential for a citizens\xe2\x80\x99 militia was an important provision for the protection of constitutional principles when a large federal government and a union of sovereign states were new, untested, and potentially dangerous concepts. Today, the idea of such a militia is unnecessary, infeasible, and antiquated. <div class="g g-3"><div class="g-single a-15"><div style="font-size: 0; display: block; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-top: 0px;"><img class="alignleft wp-image-27 size-full" style="display: block;" src="http://web.archive.org/web/20160331104550im_/http://www.thefinancialword.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Advert300.gif" alt="Advertisement" width="300" height="21"/>
