		<p class="title-newblue" style="font-size:36px; font-weight:bold; color:#333333; text-align:center; margin:0px auto;">How to Cite ProCon.org in Bibliographies<br/>
			<span class="newblue-subtitle"></span>
		</p>
        <br/>
        <br/>

		<div class="newblue-content-text"><table style="WIDTH: 96%; BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse" align="center">

<tbody>

<tr>

<td style="VERTICAL-ALIGN: top; PADDING-BOTTOM: 5px; TEXT-ALIGN: left; PADDING-TOP: 5px; PADDING-LEFT: 5px; PADDING-RIGHT: 5px">ProCon.org is the institutional or organization author for all ProCon.org pages. Proper citation depends on your preferred or required style manual. Below are the proper citation formats for ProCon.org pages according to four style manuals (in alphabetical order): <span style="FONT-STYLE: italic">Modern Language Association Style Manual</span> <span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold">(</span><span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold">MLA)</span>, <span style="FONT-STYLE: italic">The Chicago Manual of Style</span><span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold"> (Chicago)</span>, the <span style="FONT-STYLE: italic">Publication Manual of the American Psychological Association</span><span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold"> (APA)</span>, and Kate Turabian's <span style="FONT-STYLE: italic">A Manual for Writers of Term Papers, Theses, and Dissertations</span> <span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold">(Turabian)</span>.<br/>
				<br/>
				<br/>


<ol type="1">

<li><span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold">APA </span>(6th ed.):<br/>
						<br/>
						ProCon.org. (2016, February 18). Gun Control ProCon.org Retrieved from http://guncontrol.procon.org<br/>
						<br/>
						ProCon.org. (2014, August 28). School Uniforms around the World. Retrieved from<br/>
						<span style="MARGIN-LEFT: 20px">http://school-uniforms.procon.org/view.resource.php?resourceID=006010</span><br/>
						<br/>
						[Editor's Note: The APA citation style requires double spacing within entries.]<br/>
						<br/>
						<span style="FONT-STYLE: italic">[For more details on this APA citation, see "Reference List: Electronic Sources (Web Publications" at http://owl.english.purdue.edu/owl/resource/560/10/]</span><br/>
						<br/>
						</li>

<li><span style="FONT-WEIGHT: bold">Chicago </span>(16th ed.):<br/>
						<br/>
